  "skill_summaries": {
    "ultimate": "spend HP to send possessing summons onto all enemies",
    "skill1": "drain HP from the healthiest enemy",
    "skill2": "possessed summons periodically deal damage to their hosts",
    "skill3": "battle haste increase",
    "skill4": "high HP threshold triggers large AoE damage burst",
    "skill5": "summons return on possessed enemy defeat, restoring HP and energy"
  },
  "play_overview": "[[Viperian]] spends HP to send possessing summons onto every enemy, spreading pressure across the whole line. She drains HP from the healthiest foe to refill herself, while possessed summons periodically damage their hosts for sustained DoT attrition. A high-HP threshold triggers a large AoE burst, punishing healthy formations. Haste growth keeps the rotation moving, and defeated possessed enemies return summons that restore HP and Energy. This DoT and Life Drain specialist needs healing and long fights; without either, the possession loop never fully activates.",
  "counter_overview": "[[Viperian]] burns HP at battle start while Unaffected, sending DoT summons across the line; a later burst also leaves her Unaffected while casting. Do not dump opener damage into either window. Cut Vitality or healing received with [[filter:heal-inhibitor]] like [[Frieren]] or [[Gwyneth]], then delete her after possession deploys with [[filter:backline-assassin]] like [[Ravion]] or [[Nerion]]. Lasting coverage like [[Shemira]] or [[Gwyneth]] keeps pressure on before the burst lands."
}
